Presidential elections were held in the [[Serbia and Montenegro|Yugoslav]] province of [[Republic of Serbia (1992–2006)|Serbia]] on 7 December 1997, following the annulment of the results of the [[1997 Serbian general election|September–October elections]] due to low voter turnout.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://edition.cnn.com/WORLD/election.watch/europe/serbia.prez.html|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20010506181654/http://edition.cnn.com/WORLD/election.watch/europe/serbia.prez.html|url-status=dead|archive-date=6 May 2001|website=CNN|title=Serbia, FRY (Presidential)}}</ref> As no candidate won over 50% of the popular vote in the first round, a runoff was scheduled for 21 December. The result was a victory for [[Milan Milutinović]] of the [[Socialist Party of Serbia]], who defeated [[Vojislav Šešelj]] in the second round.

